swift-tui 0.10.1 imports Glibc on Linux without a Musl fallback, so pmai
cannot be built with the Swift Static Linux SDK (x86_64/aarch64-swift-linux-musl).
This patch adds the missing Musl branches next to the existing Glibc ones and
adapts the few places where musl's C types differ (SOCK_STREAM is a plain
Int32, sigaction keeps the handler in a union named __sa_handler, and environ
is imported as an optional pointer). Applied by MaiCore/scripts/build-musl.sh;
drop it once upstream swift-tui ships Musl support.

